  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.347,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.087,
            0.848,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now take any 4 numbers, place ‘+’ and ‘–’ signs in the eight different ways, and evaluate the resulting expression. What do you observe about their parities?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.143,
            0.552,
            0.163
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Repeat this with other sets of 4 numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.172,
            0.581,
            0.195
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is there a way to explain why this happens?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.151,
            0.904,
            0.204
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.817,
                0.151,
                0.904,
                0.204
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.197,
            0.8,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Think of the rules for parity of the sum or difference of two numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.24,
            0.848,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Explanation 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let us consider any of the 8 expressions formed by four numbers "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a , b , c ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and d. When one of its signs is switched, its value always increases or decreases by an even number! Let us see why."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.296,
            0.588,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider one of the expressions: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a + b - c - d ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.314,
            0.417,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Replacing +b by – b, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.438,
            0.339,
            0.559,
            0.356
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "a - b - c - d ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.362,
            0.743,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By how much has the number changed? It has changed by"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.361,
            0.386,
            0.638,
            0.405
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "( a + b - c - d ) - ( a - b - c - d )"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.415,
            0.825,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a+b-c-d-a+b+c+"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " d (notice how the signs changed when we opened the second set of brackets)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.352,
            0.464,
            0.644,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "= 2b (this is an even number)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.488,
            0.848,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the difference between two numbers is even, can they have different parities? No! So either both are even or both are odd."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.525,
            0.847,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, let us see what happens when a negative sign is switched to a positive sign."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.571,
            0.847,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Replace any negative sign in the expression a + b – c – d with a positive sign and find the difference between the two numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.62,
            0.6,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you conclude from this observation?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.65,
            0.847,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Starting from any expression, we can get 7 expressions by switching one or more ‘+’ and ‘–’ signs. Thus, all the expressions have the same parity!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.692,
            0.447,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Explanation 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We know that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.716,
            0.587,
            0.736
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_20.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{odd} \\pm \\mathrm{odd} = \\mathrm{even}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.404,
            0.742,
            0.596,
            0.76
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_21.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm { e v e n } \\pm \\mathrm { e v e n } = \\mathrm { e v e n }"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.765,
            0.587,
            0.784
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_22.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{odd} \\pm \\mathrm{even} = \\mathrm{odd}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.789,
            0.847,
            0.826
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen that the parity of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a + b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and a – b is the same, regardless of the parities of a and b."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.826,
            0.848,
            0.883
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In short, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a \\pm b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " have the same parity. By the same argument, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a \\pm b \\pm c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a \\pm b - c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " have the same parity. Extending this further, we can say that all the expressions "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a \\pm b \\pm c \\pm"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " d have the same parity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.08,
            0.915,
            0.126,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "114"
            }
          ]
        },
